  "observable_outcome": "The EARLY_WEEK1 checkpoint is now an immutable national snapshot rather than a rehearsal placeholder. Across 91 contests and five candidates the unit freezes 455 contest-candidate rows: 399 FORECAST_FROZEN, 40 ABSTAIN_UNSUPPORTED_ENTITY and 16 ABSTAIN_MISSING_REQUIRED_FEATURES. Every frozen probability pair sums to one within 1e-9, every supported margin pair sums to zero, and probability and margin directions never disagree. Expected margin and a 95% residual interval are claimed only by national_margin_ridge; every other candidate records NOT_SUPPORTED_BY_MODEL_FAMILY and UNCERTAINTY_NOT_ESTABLISHED. No frozen row is ADEQUATE_FOR_SHADOW_OBSERVATION while its opening prior is stale, so all 399 frozen rows carry LIMITED_STALE_INPUT_SHADOW_ONLY. The focus contest is discovered from the bound authority gate rather than hardcoded: the five candidates emit A and M home probabilities of 0.5, about 0.6819, about 0.8055, about 0.9182 and about 1.0000 for the base-rate, Elo, prior-only, logistic and ridge families respectively, all under LIMITED_STALE_INPUT_SHADOW_ONLY, with custom_correction_applied and tamu_specific_adjustment_applied both false. The historical fifty-percent and 68.19% rows remain immutable and are not relabelled as current. Both A and M T-24H and T-90M checkpoints remain OPEN, no Week 1 outcome is read, no candidate is recommended or promoted, and the base-rate control is never presented as recommended.",
